<section class="statues-page">
  <h1>Statues of Women and Goats in the UK</h1>

  <p>
    A London monuments audit popularised a wry fact: the capital has more statues of animals than of named women.
    This page maps <strong>women</strong> (and a few collectives) against <strong>goats</strong> — freestanding sculptures,
    woman-with-goat groups, and a short curated set of heraldic and architectural goats.
  </p>

  <p class="statues-live-summary">
    Dataset now: <strong id="live-total-count">…</strong> pins ·
    <strong id="live-women-count">…</strong> women ·
    <strong id="live-goats-count">…</strong> goats
    (counts update when the CSV loads). Aiming toward PSSA-scale coverage of named non-royal women (~180+ on their live list);
    many coordinates are still approximate — click a pin for the source link.
  </p>

  <p>
    Filter the map, zoom with the scroll wheel (or trackpad), click a marker for details, and use the nearby list when London pins pile up.
    Red family = women; blue/green/purple family = goat forms.
  </p>

  <div id="map"></div>

  <h2>How to read this</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Women</strong> mostly follow the PSSA spirit: named people in public sculpture. Royals and allegory (Queen Victoria, Boudicca, Diana fountain) are included but tagged in notes.</li>
    <li><strong>Goats</strong> are intentionally broad: public art goats, a goatherd group in Regent’s Park, an NHM relief, and one heraldic sample — not every coat of arms in Britain.</li>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> varies: street, campus, museum, rooftop, or indoor (e.g. Old Bailey tours).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Notable pins</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Millicent Fawcett</strong> — Parliament Square (first statue of a woman there)</li>
    <li><strong>Florence Nightingale</strong> — Waterloo Place</li>
    <li><strong>Edith Cavell</strong> — St Martin’s Place</li>
    <li><strong>Betty Campbell</strong> — Cardiff</li>
    <li><strong>Johann</strong> — Cushendun goat, Deborah Brown</li>
    <li><strong>I Goat</strong> — Spitalfields, Kenny Hunter</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://pssauk.org/women/">Public Statues and Sculpture Association (PSSA)</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://artuk.org/">Art UK</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://womenstatuesuk.com/">WomenstatuesUK</a></li>
    <li>CSV: <a href="/dataviz/statues.csv">/dataviz/statues.csv</a> — rebuild from <code>bun scripts/build-statues-csv.ts</code></li>
  </ul>

  <p><em>Pins with access=approx need field verification. Contributions welcome via the usual dataviz PR path.</em></p>

  {{> showSource}}
</section>

